{
  "UniqueID": "water_sawmill_placed",
  "CardName": {
    "ParentObjectID": "water_sawmill_placed",
    "LocalizationKey": "Water_Sawmill_Placed_CardName",
    "DefaultText": "Water-Driven Sawmill"
  },
  "CardDescription": {
    "ParentObjectID": "water_sawmill_placed",
    "LocalizationKey": "Water_Sawmill_Placed_CardDescription",
    "DefaultText": "A large, fixed water-powered sawmill fed by direct water or a mill race outlet."
  },
  "CardHelpSection": {
    "ParentObjectID": "water_sawmill_placed",
    "LocalizationKey": "Water_Sawmill_Placed_CardHelpSection",
    "DefaultText": "<b>Placement:</b> Build it at a river or lake, or at any outdoor location watered by a connected Mill Race Outlet. Anywhere else the build is refused.\n\n<b>Operation:</b> Drag a log onto the sawmill to Cut it into planks and wood shavings (1.5 hours).\n\n<b>Saw All:</b> Load logs into the sawmill's slots, then press Saw All (3 hours) to saw every log at once into 8 planks and 2 wood shavings each. Each log's planks keep its wood and dryness.\n\n<b>Saw Blade:</b> Every log sawn, by Cut or Saw All, adds 1 Blade Wear. At 60 the sawmill stops cutting until you drag a Copper Saw Blade onto it (Replace Saw Blade, 30 minutes), which uses the blade up. Saw All saws only as many logs as the blade has left. Packing the sawmill up keeps its wear.\n\n<b>Overshot Wheel:</b> Drag an Overshot Wheel onto the sawmill to fit it (30 minutes): Saw All then takes 1.5 hours instead of 3. Pack Up (Overshot) packs the sawmill and gives the wheel back.\n\n<b>Expand:</b> Press Expand (30 minutes) to rebuild the sawmill larger in place: its capacity grows from 20000 to 30000 weight, room for 10 logs instead of 6. Everything inside it and any fitted Overshot Wheel are kept. It costs 6 Planks and 4 Iron Nails (Metal Nails of Metal Type 200), taken from your inventory or from cards lying at this location, never from the sawmill's own slots; Expand does nothing until you hold them. Pack Up returns the plain frame, so the expansion is paid for again."
  },
